  "rationale": "With no defences, the attacker can always win. Phishing gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. pivot_internal then works because the network is not segmented. auth_appserver gives foothold_appserver, and kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin. From there: auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db, exfiltrate_db. So 0 controls is not enough. Every exfiltration technique needs admin_db, admin_fileserver or admin_backup. Each of those needs a foothold gained with stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin can only come from dump_dbadmin_dc or dump_dbadmin_adfs, which need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which can only be gained through auth_dc or auth_adfs. Both require NOT mfa_admin. Deploying mfa:admin alone therefore cuts every path, so the minimum is 1."
